**** CALL FOR POSTERS ****

The 22nd International ACM Symposium on

High-Performance Parallel and Distributed Computing

(HPDC'13)

New York City, USA - June 17-21, 2013

http://www.hpdc.org/2013

The ACM International Symposium on High-Performance Parallel and=20
Distributed Computing (HPDC)?is the premier annual conference on the=20
design, the implementation, the evaluation, and?the use of parallel and=20
distributed systems for high-end computing.HPDC'13 will take place in=20
the heart of iconic New York City from June 17-21. The conference will=20
be held on June 19-21 (Wednesday to Friday), with affiliated workshops=20
taking place on June 17-18 (Monday and Tuesday).

__

HPDC'13 will feature a poster session that will provide the right=20
environment for lively and informal discussions on various high=20
performance parallel and distributed computing topics.

We *invite all potential authors* to submit their contribution to this=20
poster session in the form of a two-page PDF abstract (we recommend=20
using the ACM Proceedings style, and fonts not smaller than 10 point).=20
Posters may be accompanied by practical demonstrations.

Participating posters will be selected based on the following criteria:

=B7Submissions must describe new, interesting ideas on any HPDC topics of=
=20
interest

=B7Submissions can present work in progress, but we strongly encourage th=
e=20
authors to include preliminary experimental results, if available

=B7Student submissions meeting the above criteria will be given preferenc=
e

Please provide the following information in your PDF file:

=B7Poster title

=B7Author names, affiliations, and email addresses

=B7Note which authors, if any, are students

=B7Indicate if you plan to set up a demo with your poster (the authors an=
d=20
organizers need to agree that the requirements for the demo to function=20
can be met at the site of the poster exhibition)

Abstracts must be submitted through EasyChair=20
(https://www.easychair.org/conferences/?conf=3Dhpdc13posters) *before May=
=20
15 2013, 23:59 EDT*. Authors will be notified of acceptance or rejection=20
via e-mail by May 20, 2013. No reviews will be provided. Posters will be=20
published online on the conference website. Each poster will have an A0=20
panel in the poster exhibition area, which will also include posters of=20
the HPDC accepted papers.

The *poster session* will be held on Wednesday, June 19, in the late=20
afternoon, and it will start with a poster advertising session during=20
which the author(s) of each poster will give a very short presentation=20
(2 slides, 1-2 minutes) of their poster. Following these presentations,=20
the poster exhibition will be opened for visiting and, we hope, for=20
fruitful discussions. Therefore, we kindly request at least one author=20
of each poster to be present throughout the entire session.

For any questions about the submission, selection, and presentation of=20
the accepted posters, please contact the Posters Chair -- Ivan Rodero,=20
Rutgers University.

--=20
